    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no registration date is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Being in `OwnerFields`, it flows into both the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (accepted on create) and `OwnerDto` (returned on read). `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 matching the existing `Pet.birthDate` pattern.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping the DTO, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null. MapStruct maps the field by name in both directions automatically.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb \u2014 used by the test suite \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency).\n\nCp07's two tests (defaults-to-today and keeps-supplied-date) pass, and the full suite remains green (14/14).",
